{#
/**
 * @file
 * The host's alert for a problem report on a page that a signed-out visitor
 * can't see.
 *
 * The page's organizers get the whole report. The host gets only this: the
 * site's name, when the report was made, the page's id and whether an
 * organizer got the report. Nothing from the page or the reporter is passed
 * to this template: no title, no address or link, no reason, no details and
 * no contact address.
 *
 * Printed inside the LocalNodes mail wrapper (email--localnodes.html.twig of
 * localnodes_platform), which supplies the greeting and the footer.
 *
 * Variables:
 * - site_name: The community's name.
 * - reported_at: When the report was made, formatted for display.
 * - nid: The reported page's id.
 * - organizers_reached: TRUE when at least one organizer got the report.
 */
#}
<p class="first-paragraph">{% trans %}Someone reported a page on {{ site_name }}.{% endtrans %}</p>
<p>{% trans %}When: {{ reported_at }}{% endtrans %}</p>
<p>{% trans %}Page id: {{ nid }}{% endtrans %}</p>
{% if organizers_reached %}
  <p>{{ "The report reached this site's organizers."|t }}</p>
{% else %}
  <p>{{ "The report could not be sent to any of this site's organizers. The person who reported it was asked to try again."|t }}</p>
{% endif %}
<p>{{ "The page isn't public, so this alert leaves out the page, the report and the reporter's details."|t }}</p>
